WEBVTT

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.990
﻿Oh no!

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.300
﻿I can't believe I forgot
﻿to set my alarm clock.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.400
﻿In the middle of a fight,
﻿Ral forgot to fight.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.740
﻿However often I see it,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.610
﻿PPSE's giant battle system
﻿is still overwhelming.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.820
﻿Good, Sei and Reiji
﻿are still fighting.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.250
﻿Huh? That's...!

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.230
﻿What's that huge Gunpla?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.300
﻿N-No way.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:22.900
﻿How come...?

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.580
﻿Sei, what's that?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.950
﻿That big one?

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.960
﻿Chairman, as you requested,

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.960
﻿we sent an auto-controlled Gunpla
﻿into the battlefield.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:49.960
﻿Thanks, babe.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.870
﻿Also, we've found out the name of
﻿the Star Build Strike's fighter.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.170
﻿It's not a full name,
﻿but he's registered as "Reiji".

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.440
﻿A-Alright.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.510
﻿His name's the same, too.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.050
﻿As I thought, Arian is...

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.890
﻿No, it can't be.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:15.860
﻿Although, if it were...!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.200
﻿Th-That looks like a 1/48
﻿Mega Size Model Zaku.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.570
﻿What the heck's going on?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.450
﻿Wh-Why?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.690
﻿There was no Gunpla like that
﻿when the battle started.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.120
- ﻿Somebody changed his machine?
﻿- I can't believe...

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.390
﻿It's moving!

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.510
﻿Mao!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.220
﻿Oh no!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.420
﻿Run!

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.230
﻿The size of that explosion...

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.560
﻿It's a Mega Size!?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.840
﻿I see. That Gunpla is
﻿an unmanned machine,

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.440
﻿stored in the battle system
﻿for playing against the computer.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.670
﻿And it's activated...!?

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.980
﻿But why?

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.250
﻿Who did this!?

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.920
﻿What happened, Kawaguchi?

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.720
﻿A Mega Size...?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.760
﻿Chairman, an unmanned Zaku
﻿is running wild in the field.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.630
﻿We should tell them to
﻿stop the battle at—

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.860
﻿No need for that.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.530
﻿What?

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.740
﻿This makes it more fun. That's all.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.840
﻿N-No... Did you send out that Zaku?

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.110
﻿Can't I?

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.980
﻿Gunpla fans all over the world are
﻿enjoying this tournament.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:22.180
﻿We should make it extravagant. Right!?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:34.500
<i>﻿The organizers have sent a large
﻿unmanned Gunpla into the battlefield.</i>

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.660
<i>﻿To avoid facing it,</i>

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.940
<i>﻿we're changing our plans
﻿to land on the ground. Stay put.</i>

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.340
﻿Roger that.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.780
﻿Oh, man. This is insane.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.640
﻿Let's get away too, brother.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.550
﻿We don't want to get involved in this.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.720
<i>﻿The large Gunpla that was
﻿sent out earlier turns out to be...</i>

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.660
<i>a surprise event
﻿prepared by the organizers.</i>

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.860
﻿What happens now?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.700
﻿I-I don't know.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:16.800
﻿But that big Gunpla looks like
﻿it's after Iori's Gunpla.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:24.480
﻿Darn!

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.450
﻿It's aiming for us, all right!

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.190
﻿Mr. Sei? What're you doing!?

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.390
﻿Get away! That Zaku has nothing
﻿to do with the battle.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.660
﻿You don't have to fight it!

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.330
﻿- <i>I know, but...</i>
﻿- <i>It's persistent!</i>

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.210
﻿You...! That's enough!

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:01.320
﻿Good, good!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.220
﻿What's that mecha called again?

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.850
﻿It's the MS-06F Zaku II.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.160
﻿Yeah, yeah. Zaku, Zaku.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.860
﻿Go for it, Zaku!

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.570
﻿Sei, what'll we do?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.000
﻿Should we discharge and escape?

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.070
<i>﻿Is that what you want?</i>

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.240
﻿No!

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:32.950
﻿Me, too. I can't stand this nonsense!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.620
﻿That's the spirit!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.480
﻿My partner!

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.430
﻿- Mr. Reiji!?
- ﻿Darn you!

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.100
- ﻿<i>Reiji, aim for the joints!</i>
- ﻿Alright!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.670
﻿Here's some more!

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.550
﻿No way...

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.620
﻿They're fighting it?

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:15.460
﻿But survival is the priority
﻿in a Battle Royale.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.390
﻿Why're they risking it for nothing?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.490
﻿They're fools...

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.830
﻿They're just like Don Quixote
﻿attacking the windmill.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.730
﻿But why...?

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.670
﻿It's obvious.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:35.940
﻿Because they're fighters!

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.810
﻿If long range is no good...

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:43.680
﻿Well go in closer!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.020
﻿A cracker!?

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.300
﻿Iori!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.880
﻿Fellini! Mao!

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.450
﻿I can't leave you guys alone.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.620
﻿I'm returning your favor!

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.220
<i>﻿Get out of my way!</i>

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.020
﻿What!?

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.690
<i>﻿Who do you think I am?</i>

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.810
<i>﻿Kawaguchi, what're you doing?</i>

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.910
﻿Destroying the Zaku!

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.650
<i>﻿You don't have to join in
﻿Chairman Mashita's game.</i>

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.350
﻿But...!

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:53.120
<i>﻿Our only goal is the championship.</i>

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.760
<i>﻿Don't forget your position.</i>

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.100
﻿I know...

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.030
<i>﻿A combined attack!</i>

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.930
<i>﻿Aim for the head!</i>

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.480
<i>﻿Yes!</i>

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.490
<i>﻿Not yet!</i>

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:27.620
﻿Then...!

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.220
﻿Reiji, discharge!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.130
﻿Got it!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.270
﻿Put all the particles into one shot!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.010
﻿No you don't!

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.890
﻿- Mao!
﻿- Fellini!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.290
﻿No!

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:18.970
﻿That machine...

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:20.910
﻿Not yet!

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.810
﻿What!?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.210
﻿Hurry!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.830
﻿Take this!!!

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.200
﻿This is...

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:24.500
﻿- Our Gunpla's power!
- ﻿Our Gunpla's power!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.410
<i>﻿Destroyed!</i>

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.180
<i>﻿The Mega Size Zaku has
﻿finally been laid to rest!</i>

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.920
﻿Sei and Reiji did it!

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.020
﻿Yeah!

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:43.290
﻿Oh, are they finally down to
﻿the required number of fighters?

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.930
﻿The buzzer for the end of
﻿the second period has sounded!

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:52.830
﻿Iori's Gunpla...

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.740
﻿I hope it's okay.

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.540
﻿How is it, Sei?

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:02.110
﻿It's fine. We have a spare shield.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.950
﻿﻿With this amount of damage,
I can fix it in one night.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.920
﻿Okay. I'm counting on you.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:11.350
﻿I know, believe me.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:11.950
﻿Mao.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.320
﻿So how's yours?

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:18.560
﻿I also have a spare satellite cannon,
﻿so I can repair it quickly.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.360
﻿Mr. Fellini told me that
﻿his isn't that bad, either.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.300
﻿That's good to hear.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.270
﻿It seems like their Gunpla are alright.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:33.640
﻿But even as a surprise event,

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.840
﻿I can't believe they sent
﻿a Mega Size Gunpla into the battle.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.180
﻿Besides, that Zaku...

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:45.420
﻿It seemed like it was only after
﻿Sei's and Reiji's Star Build Strike.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.720
﻿I might be over-thinking it, but...

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.690
﻿I still feel somewhat uneasy.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.240
﻿What do you want?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.210
﻿Ricardo Fellini.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:13.710
﻿I wanted to thank you, Nils Nielsen.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.350
﻿Thanks for your help.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:22.260
﻿Grazie, Samurai Boy.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.690
﻿No need to thank me.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:31.830
﻿I wasn't helping you guys.
﻿I just prolonged the battle,

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.470
﻿in order to study
﻿the performance of your Gunpla.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.870
﻿So was it worth it?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.170
﻿It was worth it.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:43.680
﻿Especially the features and performance...

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:47.180
﻿of the Star Build Strike built by Sei Iori.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:52.090
﻿Its shield doesn't erase
﻿the beams fired by an opponent.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:54.960
﻿When the shield's deployed,

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:58.390
﻿it alters the beam particles
﻿and absorbs them into its body.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:03.200
﻿If not, you couldn't explain
﻿the huge particle emission...

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:07.670
﻿in that last attack that
﻿destroyed the Zaku.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:13.610
﻿But now I get the principle,
﻿I can prepare for it.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:19.710
﻿If I face him in the next round,
﻿my victory will be rock-solid.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.620
﻿"Rock-solid"?

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:25.720
﻿You think you're so smart.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.150
﻿Come on, be honest.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:33.760
﻿After seeing that battle,
﻿your heart is raging, right?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.870
﻿Fighter registry name is "Reiji".

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.670
﻿It's the same name...

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.310
And if he's grown up,
he'd look like that, too.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.580
﻿The resemblance is too strong
﻿to be a coincidence.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.790
﻿But if so, why hasn't he
﻿done anything to me?

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.960
﻿Am I over-thinking it?

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.660
﻿Please stop!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:07.530
﻿You can't see the Chairman
﻿without an appointment!

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.430
﻿I said, out of my way.

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:11.560
﻿Excuse me!

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:18.340
﻿Nice to see you, Meijin Kawaguchi.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.540
﻿I hear you're doing a great job.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.940
﻿What brings you here?

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:24.780
﻿Chairman Mashita.

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.280
﻿Even if you're the tournament organizer,

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.620
﻿please refrain from selfish actions.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.680
﻿What actions?

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:34.150
﻿Oh, about that Zaku?

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.720
﻿That was good, wasn't it?

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.790
﻿Thanks to that surprise,

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.490
﻿the TV broadcast ratings
﻿went up like crazy, you know.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:44.300
﻿The sponsors were delighted, too.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:48.230
﻿Next time, your performance
﻿should make the fans roar like that.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:49.670
﻿Got it?

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.610
﻿It-It hurts!

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.510
﻿The Chairman's arm hurts!

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:57.340
﻿Please refrain from selfish actions.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.010
﻿Meijin, that's enough!

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.980
﻿Chairman, please refrain from—

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.690
﻿Okay okay. I won't do it anymore!

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.720
﻿Okay then.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.230
﻿Sorry for interrupting.
﻿Excuse me.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.930
﻿- Are you alright, Chairman?
- ﻿Ouch!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.970
﻿My arm hurts!
﻿Please make this pain fly away.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.640
﻿Pain, pain, fly away!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.180
﻿I feel great now!

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:32.080
﻿Oh man...

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.980
﻿Chairman Mashita can be
﻿such a troublemaker.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.520
﻿He's so disrespectful.

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:39.420
﻿I can't stand such selfish actions.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.920
﻿But you're selfish, too.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:44.320
﻿What do you mean?

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.830
﻿Don't play dumb with me.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:49.260
﻿When the Mega Size Zaku
﻿was running wild...

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.100
﻿You helped them, right?

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:58.410
﻿Using your long range sniper rifle.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.580
﻿I could tell by looking at the beam.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:05.650
﻿After all, I designed that rifle myself.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:08.950
﻿Then let me say...

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:13.250
﻿What's the value of winning
﻿by defeating a damaged Gunpla?

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.820
﻿It's not enough just to win.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:21.960
﻿A Meijin should crush opponents
﻿when they're at their best.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.970
﻿In order to prove that,
﻿I won't budge an inch.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.880
﻿Sei, it's dinner time.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.810
﻿I'm gonna keep working.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:42.480
﻿Reiji, are you going out
﻿for snacks again tonight?

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.020
﻿When you go to the store,
﻿get me something too.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.290
﻿Gotcha!

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:59.230
﻿The Absorb System, which alters
﻿and absorbs enemy particle beams...

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.770
﻿Not only does Mr. Luang know its secret,

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.880
﻿but I should assume that
﻿other fighters already know, too.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:16.780
﻿Also about the Discharge System,
﻿which releases all the absorbed particles.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:23.520
﻿Depending on the situation,
we may have to use...

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:29.800
﻿the third system after the
﻿Absorb System and Discharge System.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.840
﻿Thank you.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.720
﻿What's this? Meat buns?

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:53.850
﻿You gave me too much money last time.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.690
﻿I'm making up the difference.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.390
﻿You...?

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.930
﻿You were waiting for me
﻿this whole time, just for this?

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.760
﻿I didn't want to keep on owing you.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:07.430
﻿So I paid you back right away.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.300
﻿Huh? What?

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:14.270
﻿I don't want it. It's cold already.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:17.480
﻿It's not my fault. I didn't know
﻿when you were coming!

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.680
﻿So who asked you to wait?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.920
﻿- Take it!
﻿- Don't want it.

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:26.250
﻿But I want to pay you back!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.000
﻿Look at them.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:41.200
﻿What're you kids flirting about?

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.500
﻿"No, we can't do it here."

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:48.510
﻿What did you say, idiots!?

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.350
Eh?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.650
﻿Who do you think you're talking to?

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:59.020
﻿Hey, do you mind?

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.490
﻿Oh, man.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:07.890
﻿Stop trying to show off
﻿in front of your girlfriend, kid!

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:49.200
﻿Chairman.

00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:56.070
﻿Why are you so concerned
﻿about that boy Reiji?

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:59.210
﻿Do l have to tell you why?

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:02.210
﻿If you don't want to, that's fine,

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:05.210
﻿I'll just do as you say.

00:23:05.210 --> 00:23:06.480
﻿Then do that.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:08.480
﻿So how's it going?

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:11.350
﻿As you requested,

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:17.920
﻿I've set up Sei Iori's and Reiji's
﻿opponent for the upcoming third period.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:22.830
﻿Their opponent's the Thai champion,

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:26.200
﻿Luang Dallara.

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:29.170
﻿Their defeat is inevitable.

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:34.470
﻿This boy can't be the prince.

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:43.020
﻿But it's a real eyesore to have
﻿a boy with that face around here.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.410
﻿We fight Luang Dallara,
﻿a tough opponent.

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.900
﻿Sei, what the heck is this weapon?

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:00.910
